 CHAPTER 13 OF THE UNITED STATES CODE

Title 11--Bankruptcy

Subtitle V--Discharge

Section 1327

(a) Discharge of Debtor

(1) Effective Date

An individual debtor's discharge under section 1328 of this title shall become effective upon the date of entry of the order approving the plan, unless the court orders otherwise.

(2) Notice Required Before Discharge

Before the court grants a discharge under section 1328 of this title, notice shall be given to the trustee and to each creditor whose claim is affected by the discharge. The notice shall inform the recipient that a motion for a stay of the discharge pending appeal may be made within thirty days after receipt of the notice.

(3) Stay of Proceedings During Appeal

If a motion for a stay of the discharge pending appeal is timely filed, the court shall enter a stay of the discharge until the resolution of the appeal. Upon the final disposition of the appeal, the court shall enter an order vacating the discharge and ordering the clerk of the court to notify the trustee and each creditor whose claim is affected by the discharge that the discharge has been vacated.

(4) Final Judgment on Appeal

Upon the final disposition of an appeal concerning a discharge under section 1328 of this title, the court shall enter a final judgment on the appeal.

(5) Time Limitation for Filing Motion for Reconsideration

No motion for reconsideration of a final judgment entered pursuant to subsection (4) of this section may be filed later than ninety days after the entry of the judgment.

(6) Effect of Discharge

A discharge under section 1328 of this title releases the debtor from all debts that were incurred before the date of the filing of the petition for relief, except--

(A) Any debt that is excluded from discharge under section 1328(a)(1) of this title;

(B) Any debt that is not properly identified in the schedules filed by the debtor;

(C) Any debt that is owed to a government unit;

(D) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was insolvent at the time the extension of credit was made;

(E) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was unable to pay the debt at the time the extension of credit was made;

(F) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was engaged in fraudulent activity at the time the extension of credit was made;

(G) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was involved in illegal activities at the time the extension of credit was made;

(H) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was involved in terrorist activities at the time the extension of credit was made;

(I) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was involved in organized crime at the time the extension of credit was made;

(J) Any debt that is owed to a person who has extended credit to the debtor in good faith and without knowledge that the debtor was involved in drug trafficking at the time the extension of credit was made;

